@label I. Allegro con brio
@note F minor. A terse motto in octaves (a dotted rise through the tonic chord to D flat, falling to C) drives the movement; it keeps muttering in the basses under the lyrical second theme in A flat. The development includes a fugato on the motto; the second theme returns in F major before the motto pulls the coda back to the minor.
@meter 4/4
@tempo "Allegro con brio" 1/4=132
@key Fm
% The motto in octaves, full orchestra
@def MOTTO
vc: [M:4/4] !ff!F,3 G, _A,2 C2 | !sfz!_D4 C2 z2 | _B,3 C _D2 F2 | !sfz!G4 E2 z2 |
v1: = vc +P8
v2: = vc +P8
va: = vc
cb: = vc -P8
bn: = vc
cl: = vc +P8
ob: = vc +P8
fl: = vc +P15
hn: !ff!C2 z6 | z4 C2 z2 | F2 z6 | z4 [CE]2 z2 |
tp: !ff!c2 z6 | z4 c2 z2 | f2 z6 | z4 c2 z2 |
tm: !ff!F,,2 z6 | z4 C,2 z2 | F,,2 z6 | z4 C,2 z2 |
@end

% The motto quietly in the first violins over pulsing violas, then a falling scale and a full close
@def T1B
v1: !p!f3 g _a2 c'2 | _d'4 c'2 z2 | _b3 c' _d'2 f'2 | g'4 e'2 z2 |
v2: !p!c8 | _d4 c2 z2 | _d8 | _B4 _B2 z2 |
va: !p!_A_A_A_A _A_A_A_A | FFFF EE z2 | FFFF FFFF | EEEE EE z2 |
vc: !p!F,2 z2 F,2 z2 | _B,,2 z2 C,2 z2 | _B,,2 z2 _B,,2 z2 | C,2 z2 C,2 z2 |
cb: = vc -P8

@def T1B2
